    "summary": "I built four full bases in two pairs. Pair A is at (0,0) and (1,0), and pair B is at (0,1) and (1,1). Each pair is held together by one joint bolt. The two pairs touch along three walls, and each of those walls has a single side connector and no bolt, so the connectors are the only thing joining the pairs. I added solid end caps on all 14 open faces. I didn't run lockJoints because it would have bolted the walls between the pairs. The check found no rule errors and the mesh check came back clear. It gave one warning, LOOSE_BODY: it says pair B could slide away from pair A because no bolt locks them. That's what you'd expect when the pairs are joined only by side connectors. I added no props, since you didn't mention a use for the build.",
